    <group name="func_character_block" color="0.42745098039215684 0.5568627450980392 0.5725490196078431">
        <string key="classname" name="Classname" value="func_character_block">The classname of the entity.</string>
    </group>
    <group name="navBlock" color="0.2 0.2 0.2">
        <string key="classname" name="Classname" value="navBlock">The classname of the entity.</string>
    </group>
    <point name="logic_once" color="0.6 0.1 0.7" box="-4 -4 -4 4 4 4">
        <string key="targetname" name="Name" />
        <string key="classname" name="Classname" value="logic_once">The classname of the entity.</string>
    </point>
    <point name="counter" color="1 1 0.4" box="-16 -16 -32 16 16 16">
        <integer key="startNum" name="Start Number" value="0" />
        <integer key="targetNum" name="Target Number" value="0" />
        <target key="target" name="Target" />
        <string key="onReached" name="On Reached" value="reached" />
        <string key="targetname" name="Name" />
        <string key="classname" name="Classname" value="counter">The classname of the entity.</string>
        <angle key="angle" name="Yaw Angle" value="0">Yaw rotation in degrees. 0 = East, 90 = South, etc.</angle>
        <angles key="angles" name="Pitch Yaw Roll" value="0 0 0">Full rotation: Pitch Yaw Roll in degrees.</angles>
        <integer key="spawnflags" name="Spawnflags" value="0">Bitmask of spawning flags.</integer>
        <flag key="no_dificuly_easy" name="Don't spawn on Easy" bit="0" />
        <flag key="no_dificuly_normal" name="Don't spawn on Normal" bit="1" />
        <flag key="no_dificuly_hard" name="Don't spawn on Hard" bit="2" />
    </point>
    <point name="spawner" color="1 0.2 0.8" box="-16 -16 -32 16 16 16">
        <string key="className" name="Class Name" value="npc_base" />
        <boolean key="autoTrigger" name="Auto Trigger" value="npc_base" />
        <string key="targetname" name="Name" />
        <target key="target" name="Target" />
        <angles key="angles" name="Rotation" value="0 0 0" />
        <angle key="angle" name="Rotation" value="0" />
        <string key="onSpawned" name="On Spawn" value="spawned" />
        <string key="onDespawned" name="On Despawn" value="despawned" />
        <string key="classname" name="Classname" value="spawner">The classname of the entity.</string>
        <integer key="spawnflags" name="Spawnflags" value="0">Bitmask of spawning flags.</integer>
        <flag key="no_dificuly_easy" name="Don't spawn on Easy" bit="0" />
        <flag key="no_dificuly_normal" name="Don't spawn on Normal" bit="1" />
        <flag key="no_dificuly_hard" name="Don't spawn on Hard" bit="2" />
    </point>
    <point name="transformPoint" color="0 0 0" box="-3 -3 -3 3 3 3">
        <angles key="angles" name="Rotation" value="0 0 0" />
        <string key="targetname" name="Name" />
        <string key="classname" name="Classname" value="transformPoint">The classname of the entity.</string>
        <angle key="angle" name="Yaw Angle" value="0">Yaw rotation in degrees. 0 = East, 90 = South, etc.</angle>
        <integer key="spawnflags" name="Spawnflags" value="0">Bitmask of spawning flags.</integer>
        <flag key="no_dificuly_easy" name="Don't spawn on Easy" bit="0" />
        <flag key="no_dificuly_normal" name="Don't spawn on Normal" bit="1" />
        <flag key="no_dificuly_hard" name="Don't spawn on Hard" bit="2" />
    </point>
    <point name="music_player" color="0.6 0.12 0.6" box="-15 -15 -15 15 15 15">
        <string key="bankName" name="Sound Bank" value="Music.bank" />
        <string key="eventName" name="Event Name" />
        <real key="volume" name="Volume" value="0.5" />
        <real key="fadeTime" name="Fade Time" value="1" />
        <string key="targetname" name="Name" />
        <string key="classname" name="Classname" value="music_player">The classname of the entity.</string>
    </point>
    <!-- ================================================================================================
         SimGame: living world simulation. Read by the world nav bake (sim_portal, sim_spawn) and by the
         sim bridge. Ids marked "stable" are saved in game saves: never rename or reuse them once a level ships.
         ================================================================================================ -->
    <point name="sim_spawn" color="0 1 0" box="-16 -16 -24 16 16 32">
Arrival point for level transitions, and the player start. A sim_portal in another level names it in targetSpawn. Keep it a few metres inside the level from the sim_portal that leads back, on walkable ground, facing into the level.
        <string key="targetname" name="Name">Unique in this level. sim_portal.targetSpawn refers to it.</string>
        <angle key="angle" name="Yaw Angle" value="0" />
        <integer key="spawnflags" name="Spawnflags" value="0">Bitmask of spawning flags.</integer>
        <flag key="player_start" name="Default player start" bit="0">Used when the level is loaded directly (-map), not through a portal.</flag>
        <string key="classname" name="Classname" value="sim_spawn">The classname of the entity.</string>
    </point>
    <group name="sim_portal" color="0.3 0.6 1">
Level transition trigger. The player loads targetLevel and lands at targetSpawn. NPCs use the same transition through the world nav mesh: the bake links this trigger's centre to targetSpawn. The brush centre must be on or just above walkable ground (the bake searches 4 m up and down, 2 m sideways). One trigger per direction: the target level needs its own sim_portal back.
        <string key="targetname" name="Name">Unique in this level; used in bake messages.</string>
        <string key="targetLevel" name="Target Level" value="village.bsp">Map file name inside GameData/maps, as listed in the world manifest.</string>
        <string key="targetSpawn" name="Target Spawn">targetname of a sim_spawn in the target level.</string>
        <boolean key="_cs" name="Cast Shadows" value="0" />
        <string key="classname" name="Classname" value="sim_portal">The classname of the entity.</string>
    </group>
    <group name="sim_settlement" color="0.8 0.7 0.2">
Volume of a settlement (village, town district). Sites inside belong to it: notice boards, candidate searches and reputation are per settlement.
        <string key="settlementId" name="Settlement Id (stable)">Unique across the whole world, e.g. ashby.</string>
        <string key="displayName" name="Display Name" />
        <boolean key="_cs" name="Cast Shadows" value="0" />
        <string key="classname" name="Classname" value="sim_settlement">The classname of the entity.</string>
    </group>
    <group name="sim_site" color="0.9 0.5 0.1">
A place that matters to the simulation (design section 5.2): house, pub, bakery, church, shop, field, well, market, graveyard, station. The brush is its footprint (ownership, privacy). Agents enter through its sim_door points; inside they are counted by occupancy and slots, not positions.
        <string key="siteId" name="Site Id (stable)">Unique across the whole world, e.g. ashby_crooked_lamp.</string>
        <string key="kind" name="Kind" value="house">Site template id from the sim data (house, pub, bakery, church, shop, field, well, market, graveyard, station, ...).</string>
        <string key="displayName" name="Display Name" />
        <integer key="capacity" name="Capacity" value="0">Maximum occupants; 0 takes the kind's default.</integer>
        <boolean key="_cs" name="Cast Shadows" value="0" />
        <string key="classname" name="Classname" value="sim_site">The classname of the entity.</string>
    </group>
    <point name="sim_door" color="1 0.6 0.2" box="-12 -12 0 12 12 48">
Entrance of a site: where agents enter and exit. Place it on walkable ground just outside the doorway. A site can have several.
        <string key="site" name="Site Id">siteId of the sim_site it opens into.</string>
        <string key="door" name="Physical Door">Optional targetname of the func_door whose lock state mirrors this entrance.</string>
        <angle key="angle" name="Yaw Angle (facing out)" value="0" />
        <string key="classname" name="Classname" value="sim_door">The classname of the entity.</string>
    </point>
    <point name="sim_slot" color="0.7 0.4 1" box="-10 -10 0 10 10 40">
A typed position inside a site (seat, bed, work, counter, queue, stand). The sim counts slots; bodies use the exact spot when the level is loaded.
        <string key="site" name="Site Id">siteId of the sim_site it belongs to.</string>
        <string key="slotType" name="Slot Type" value="seat">seat, bed, work, counter, queue, stand, or a type from the sim data.</string>
        <angle key="angle" name="Yaw Angle" value="0" />
        <string key="classname" name="Classname" value="sim_slot">The classname of the entity.</string>
    </point>
    <point name="sim_container" color="0.6 0.4 0.2" box="-12 -12 0 12 12 32">
A container prop whose contents are simulated items (addendum section 9): shelf, pantry, cashbox, barrel, wardrobe, crate. Everything else in a level is static scenery.
        <string key="containerId" name="Container Id (stable)">Unique across the whole world, e.g. ashby_bakery_shelf_1.</string>
        <string key="site" name="Site Id">siteId of the sim_site it belongs to (optional for containers in the open).</string>
        <string key="containerType" name="Container Type" value="shelf">shelf, pantry, cashbox, barrel, wardrobe, crate, or a type from the sim data.</string>
        <string key="access" name="Access" value="owner">owner, household, staff or public.</string>
        <model key="model" name="Model Path" />
        <real key="modelscale" name="Uniform Scale" value="1" />
        <angle key="angle" name="Yaw Angle" value="0" />
        <string key="classname" name="Classname" value="sim_container">The classname of the entity.</string>
    </point>
    <point name="sim_npc" color="0.9 0.9 0.3" box="-16 -16 -32 16 16 32">
Starting place of an authored NPC (priest, doctor, publican...). Generated population needs no entities; it comes from sites.
        <string key="npcId" name="NPC Id (stable)">Authored NPC id from the sim data.</string>
        <angle key="angle" name="Yaw Angle" value="0" />
        <string key="classname" name="Classname" value="sim_npc">The classname of the entity.</string>
    </point>
</classes>
